 ### [DiffusioNeRF](8703-diffusionerf.md)
-DiffusioNeRF is a NeRF optimization procedure that incorporates a denoising diffusion model to learn priors for scene geometry and color, improving reconstruction quality under sparse input views. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF training by rendering random RGBD patches and backpropagating the estimated gradients of their log-likelihood to the color and density fields, effectively normalizing the scene representation.
+DiffusioNeRF is a method that integrates a denoising diffusion model (DDM) as an initial learning factor to standardize the training of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF). It utilizes the DDM to learn priors for scene geometry and color, normalizing these fields to achieve higher quality reconstruction, particularly under sparse input views. Unlike standard NeRF which relies solely on photometric consistency, DiffusioNeRF steers the optimization by backpropagating gradients derived from the diffusion model's likelihood estimates.
 
